cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "BraggTrack"
type: software
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-05-16"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/BASE-Laboratory/BraggTrack"
url: "https://github.com/BASE-Laboratory/BraggTrack"
abstract: >-
  Semantic 4D kinematics, multi-scan gap closing, chemomechanical fracture
  tracking, operando electrochemistry synchronization, and online autonomous
  Dark-Field X-ray Microscopy (DFXM) target selection for operando X-ray
  diffraction. BraggTrack segments Bragg reflections in 3D reciprocal-space
  volumes, tracks trajectories and split/merge lineage with analytical
  uncertainties using classical crystallography and batched vision-transformer
  embeddings, and exports ImageD11, NeXus HDF5, BLISS zoom triggers, and
  interactive HTML 4D lineage reports.
keywords:
  - X-ray diffraction
  - dark-field X-ray microscopy
  - operando crystallography
  - autonomous experiments
  - 3D segmentation
  - object tracking
  - grain fracture
  - synchrotron
  - materials science
  - Python
authors:
